2. Free individual use

An individual may, without a fee, download, install, use, copy, study, and
modify the Software for that individual's own use. This includes reading and
sending the individual's work-related email and use by employees or independent
professionals on their own initiative. An email account's domain or the business
subject of a message does not, by itself, make this individual use commercial
licensing use under section 3.

The individual-use grant cannot be used as a substitute for a license covering
an enterprise deployment or commercial integration, distribution, or sale.

3. Uses requiring separate commercial authorization

Prior written authorization from the relevant Anser copyright holders is
required for:

(a) deployment by or on behalf of an enterprise, including centralized rollout,
    bulk installation, management, or requiring the Software as part of the
    enterprise's systems or tools for employees or customers;
(b) incorporating the Software or substantial Anser-owned portions of it into
    a commercial product, platform, service, or hosted offering; and
(c) selling, renting, sublicensing for a fee, or commercially distributing the
    Software or a product or service that provides its functionality.

Enterprise deployment requires authorization even when the Software itself is
not sold. Merely recommending the Software to colleagues, who independently
choose to install and use it under section 2, is not a centralized enterprise
deployment. Charges, quantities, duration, support, and other commercial terms
must be agreed separately in writing; they are not promised by this license.

4. Noncommercial sharing and changes

Copies of the Software, including modified copies, may be shared without a fee
for uses permitted by this license. All copies must retain this license and
applicable copyright and third-party notices. Modified distributions must
clearly identify that they are modified and must not claim to be an official
Anser release. Sharing does not grant recipients rights to a use requiring
commercial authorization under section 3. Anser trademarks or an endorsement
are not granted by this license.

5. User content

This license governs the Software, not users' email, attachments, signatures,
